    "ls|LS17_S6_U_269": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 269  \nANSWERED ON 20.07.2021 \n  \nFUNDS RELEASED FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ  \n  \n269.       MS. S. JOTHIMANI \nWill the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n(a) the budgetary outlay for Panchayati Raj institutions made for Financial Year 2020-2021; \n(b) the details of funds released for Panchayati Raj in the Financial Year 2019- 2020 and 2020-\n2021, State-wise; \n(c) whether there are dues pending in the allocation of funds to the State of  Tamil Nadu; and \n(d) if so, the reasons thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL) \n \n(a)  A sum of Rs.690.00 crore (Revised Estimate) was provided to Ministry of Panchayati Raj \n(MoPR) for the year 2020-21, out of which Rs.546.94 crore was allocated for strengthening \nPanchayati Raj Institutions and incentivisation for their developmental works under the  \nCentrally Sponsored Scheme-Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA) and Incentivisation of \nPanchayats, a Central component of RGSA.  Under the Fifteenth Finance Commission Award, \nan amount of Rs.60750 crore was allocated to Panchayati Raj Institutions during 2020-21.   \n(b)    The State-wise release of funds under the schemes of Ministry of Panchayati Raj (MoPR) \nand out of awards of Fourteenth Finance Commission and Fifteenth Finance Commission are \ngiven at Annexure.   \n(c) No prior allocation of funds is made to any States under the Schemes of Ministry of \nPanchayati Raj. The funds under the RGSA Scheme is released based on the annual action plan \nsubmitted by the State concerned including the State of Tamil Nadu and funds under the \nscheme of Incentivisation of Panchyats is released to the best performing Panchayats selected \nthrough a national competition for the National Panchayat Awards of various categories.    For \nthe State of Tamil Nadu, dues of Central Finance Commission Grants are not pending as the \naward period 2015 -20 of Fourteenth Finance Commission (XIV FC) is already over and the \n\nFifteenth Finance Commission (XV FC) Grants have been released upto the first installment \nof Basic (Untied) Grants for FY 2021-22. \n(d) Does not arise in view of (c) above.   \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to part (b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.269 \nAnswered on 20.07.2021 regarding ‘Funds Released for Panchayati Raj’ \n \nState-wise release of funds under the Scheme Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan during \n2019-20 and 2020-21 \n \n \n \n \n \nSl. No. State/ UTs 2019-20 \n(Rs. in crore) \n2020-21 \n(Rs. in crore) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 0 22.339 \n2 Andaman  & Nicobar Islands 0 0 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 39.59 0 \n4 Assam 23.22 26.1159 \n5 Bihar 0 0 \n6 Chhattisgarh 0 4.0395 \n7 Dadra & Nagar Haveli 0 0 \n8 Daman & Diu 0 0 \n9 Goa 0 0 \n10 Gujarat 0 0 \n11 Haryana 0 9.89 \n12 Himachal Pradesh 10 22.098 \n13 Jammu & Kashmir 6.19 25.00 \n14 Jharkhand 0 2.34 \n15 Karnataka 0 0.439 \n16 Kerala 0 8.12955 \n17 Lakshadweep 0 0 \n18 Ladakh  2.1485 \n19 Madhya Pradesh 85.48 71.42 \n20 Maharashtra 8.44 66.76 \n21 Manipur 4.54 3.4127 \n22 Meghalaya 2.63 3.967 \n23 Mizoram 0.5 21.185 \n24 Nagaland 3.94 3.7217 \n25 Odisha 0 2.937 \n26 Punjab 0 13.45 \n27 Rajasthan 0 12.981 \n28 Sikkim 5.1 4.7475 \n29 Tamil Nadu 5.3 56.875 \n30 Telangana 0 12 \n31 Tripura 0 2.5304 \n32 Uttar Pradesh 169.92 32.54 \n33 Uttarakhand 23.79 26.751 \n34 West Bengal 44.10 33.52 \n Total 432.74 491.3378 \n\nState-wise release of funds under the Scheme of Incentivization of Panchayats during \n2019-20 and 2020-21 \n  \n(Amount Rs. in crores) \nSl. No. States/ UTs 2019-20 2020-21 \n1.  Andaman & Nicobar Islands 0.05 0.18 \n2.  Andhra Pradesh 2.20 2.47 \n3.  Arunachal Pradesh 0.50 0.15 \n4.  Assam 0.97 1.59 \n5.  Bihar 0.25 2.76 \n6.  Chhattisgarh 1.55 1.54 \n7.  Dadra & Nagar haveli 0 0.70 \n8.  Daman & Diu 0 0.35 \n9.  Goa 0 0 \n10.  Gujarat 0.05 3.62 \n11.  Haryana 0.05 2.86 \n12.  Himachal Pradesh 1.33 1.54 \n13.  Jammu & Kashmir 0.05 0.60 \n14.  Jharkhand 1.36 1.52 \n15.  Karnataka 1.63 0.10 \n16.  Kerala 0.25 1.75 \n17.  Ladakh 0 0 \n18.  Lakshadweep 0 0.05 \n19.  Madhya Pradesh 2.35 0.05 \n20.  Maharashtra 0 2.31 \n21.  Manipur 0.78 0.25 \n22.  Meghalaya 0.05 0 \n23.  Mizoram 0 0 \n24.  Nagaland 0 0.26 \n25.  Odisha 0 2.97 \n26.  Punjab 1.62 1.64 \n27.  Rajasthan 1.34 1.83 \n28.  Sikkim 0.81 0.86 \n29.  Tamil Nadu 0.05 3.56 \n30.  Telangana 0.05 2.91 \n31.  Tripura 1.06 1.36 \n32.  Uttarakhand 0.05 2.96 \n33.  Uttar Pradesh 4.70 4.79 \n34.  West Bengal 1.60 1.65 \nTotal 24.70 49.18 \n  \n\n \nState-wise releases made out of awards of of Fourteenth Finance Commission and \nFifteenth Finance Commission Grants to the States for Gram Panchayats during 2019-\n20 and 2020-21 respectively.  \n \nSL. No. State Release \n(Rs. in crore) \n2019-20 2020-21 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 2336.56 2625.00 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 221.38 231.00 \n3 Assam 1462.45 1604.00 \n4 Bihar 5674.7 5018.00 \n5 Chhattisgarh 1415.89 1454.00 \n6 Goa 36.12 37.50 \n7 Gujarat 2331.33 3195.00 \n8 Haryana 1048.53 1264.00 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 488.64 429.00 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir# -  \n11 Jharkhand 1632.59 1689.00 \n11 Karnataka 2504.1309 3217.00 \n12 Kerala 1084.73 1628.00 \n13 Madhya Pradesh 3660.14 3984.00 \n14 Maharashtra 4059.55 5827.00 \n15 Manipur 55.63 177.00 \n16 Meghalaya *           91.00 \n17 Mizoram * 93.00 \n18 Nagaland * 62.50 \n19 Odisha 2389.54 2258.00 \n20 Punjab 1104.58 1388.00 \n21 Rajasthan 3681.01 3862.00 \n22 Sikkim 40.09 42.00 \n23 Tamil Nadu 1821.106 3607.00 \n24 Telangana 1451.3 1847.00 \n25 Tripura 90.625 191.00 \n26 Uttar Pradesh 9659.47 9752.00 \n\n27 Uttarakhand 508.31 574.00 \n28 West Bengal 3703.2504 4412.00 \n  Total 52461.65 60559.00 \n # Jammu & Kashmir converted into UT     \n* No Fourteenth Finance Commission Awards as these states are in non-part IX areas.  \n  \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_270": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n270\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n20\nTH\n \nJULY\n, 2021\n \n \nADJUDICATING DISPUTES UNDER NEW FARM LAWS\n \n270\n.  \nSHRI \nT.N. PRATHAPAN:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS\n \n \nWELFARE   \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has barred civil courts\n \nfrom adjudicating disputes \n \nunder the Farmers‘ Produce\n \nTrade and Commerce (Promotion & Facilitation) \n \nAct 2020\n \nand the Farmers (Empowerment and Protection)\n \nAgreement on \n \nPrice Assurance and Farm Services Act\n \n2020 and transferred the same to \n \nexecutive officers, if so,\n \nthe reasons therefor;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the \naforementioned executive officers\n \nincluding Sub\n-\nDivisional \n \nMagistrates and Collectors are\n \nequipped to adjudicate on contentious legal \n \nand\n \ncontractual disputes emanating from these legislations;\n \nand\n \n \n(c) \n \nif so, the details thereof including the justifica\ntion\n \nof the same?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS\n \nWELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH\n \nTOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to (c)\n:\n \nIn order to resolve the disputes relating to Farm Acts under Farmers’ \nProduce Trade and Commerce (Promotion &\n \nFacilitation) Act 2020, and Farmers \n(Empowerment and Protection) Agreement on Price Assurance and Farm Services \nAct 2020, a quick and \ncost effective dispute resolution mechanism is prescribed for \nthe farmers at sub\n-\ndivision level through conciliation boar\nd and further by Sub\n-\nDivisional Authority and District Collector.  \n \n \n \nThe executive officers at Sub Divisional level and District Collectors perform \nthe functions relating to land revenue including maintaining land records and \nresolving the disputes relati\nng to crops and land.  Thus, they have sufficient field \nexperiences relating to agriculture & land disputes as well as on  judicial practices.  \nIn view of the above, they are more equipped to adjudicate on all legal and \ncontractual disputes emanating from \nthese Farm Legislations.\n \n \n*****\n \n ",
