    "ls|LS17_S6_U_285": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n285\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n2\n0\nTH\n \n \nJULY\n \n2021\n \n \nLOW PENETRATION OF CROP INSURANCE \n \n \n285\n.\n \n   \nSHRI SRIDHAR KOTAGIRI: \n \n \n   \nSHRIMATI CHINTA ANURADHA: \n \n \n   \nSHRI POCHA BRAHMANANDA REDDY: \n \n \n   \nSHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR BELLANA:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) whether the Government has recently identified 75 aspirational/tribal districts in the \ncountry where crop insurance penetration is very low; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State\n-\nwise; and \n \n(c) the measures taken by the Government to ensure an increas\ne in crop insurance \npenetration among farmers?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to (c) :  Yes Sir. \n \nA structured\n \nawareness campaign ‘Crop Insurance Week/Fasal Bima \nSaptah’ was \ninitiated by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare between 1st July \n2021 to 7\nth\n \nJuly 2021 under Azadi Ka Amrit Mahotsav\n, \n \nan initiative to celebrate 75 years \nof India’s independence, in all the\n \ndistricts/areas notified under\n \nPradhan Mantri Fasal \nBima Yojana (PMFBY)/Restructured Weather Based Crop Insurance Scheme (RWBCIS) \nwith special emphasis on 75 aspirational/tribal districts\n.\n  \nThe State\n-\nwise details of \nselected 75 aspirational/tribal districts is \nannexed\n.\n \n  \nT\nhe\n \ncore focus o\nf the campaign was \nt\no increase\n \nthe \nawareness\n \nand benefits of the scheme\n,\n \nsensitize the stakeholders and to \nincrease overall\n \nenrollment of farmers, \nthereby helping them \nto \nreap the benefits\n \nof crop \ninsurance\n \nwith special focus on\n \nidentified aspirational/tribal d\nistricts\n. \n \nT\no \nincrease the \ncrop insurance penetration t\nhe campaign strategy aimed at: \n \n \ni\n.\n \nM\nobilization of multi\n-\nlevel stakeholders \nfor successful implementation of \nCrop \nInsurance Week \nviz\n \nStat\nes/UTs\n, \nB\nanks, \nCommon Service Centers (\nCSCs\n)\n, \nI\nnsurance \nC\nompanies\n(ICs)\n \nincluding\n \ngrassroot level association with \nAgricultural \nTechnology Management Agency (\nATMA\n)\n \nfunctionaries\n, Panchayati Raj Institutions \n\n(PRI), \nFamer Producer  Organizations (\nFPO\ns\n)\n,\n \nPrimary Agricultural Credit Society \n(\nPACS\n) etc.\n \nii\n.\n \nA \n360\n-\ndegree execution plan of all \nIn\nformation, Education and Communication \n(\nIEC\n)\n \nactivities at the grassroots level through channels such as awareness \nvehicles, TV shows, print media, digital media, \n \nOut of Home (\nOOH\n) advertising\n, \nbehavioral change communication (Nukkad Nataks), etc.\n \niii\n.\n \nA\n \nuniform communication, key messages, and branding across all kharif 2021 \nnotified locations\n.\n  \n \nThe campaign was launched by \nthe\n \nUnion Minister for \nAgriculture and Farmers \nwelfare \nalong with\n \nrelease\n \nof\n \nPMFBY e\n-\nBrochure, FAQ Booklet and a \nPMFBY/RWBICS Guide\nbook to assist farmers and ground level coordinators in \nunderstanding the basics of the scheme. \n \nDuring the entire duration of the campaign, farmers were engaged through multiple \nIEC activities with\n \nthe\n \nsupport of State Government and local level organizat\nions viz \nAgricultural Technology Management Agency (\nATMA\n)\n \nfunctionaries\n, Panchayati Raj \nInstitutions (PRI), \nFa\nr\nmer Producer  Organizations (\nFPOs\n)\n, Banks,\n \nPri\nmary \nAgricultural Credit Societies\n \n(\nPACS\n),\n \nCommon Service Centers (CSCs), \nI\nnsurance \nC\nompanies\n \n(ICs)\n.\n \nFollowing are the grassroot activities undertaken in the above\n-\nmentioned \nS\ntates to \ncreate widespread awareness\n \nand to increase crop insurance penetration\n \nduring \nthis week:\n \ni\n.\n \nA total of 24 IEC Vans travelled in all 75 blocks of 75 Districts during kharif \n2021 \ninforming farmers on benefit of crop insurance, enrolment process and other \nscheme related information.\n \nClose to 500 vans were additionally deployed by \nInsurance Companies at individual level in other districts.\n \nii\n.\n \nMore than 16 thousand ground level IEC \nactivities viz farmer meeting, village \nlevel sensitization activities were reported by various stakeholders. \n \niii\n.\n \nA total of \n5\n \ncrore audio \ncalls \nwere sent to farmers of all districts including \naspirational and tribal districts. \n \niv\n.\n \nDistribution of PMFBY print \nmat\nerial \nsuch as pamphlets, flyers across entire \ndistricts and blocks\n.\n \nv\n.\n \nSpecial engagement workshop/seminars with Women Farmers\n \nvi\n.\n \nBanners and Wall Paintings \n \nvii\n.\n \nNukkad Natak done in various villages/ blocks\n \nviii\n.\n \nDisplay of Hoardings/Posters in Hindi and other regional l\nanguages \n \nix\n.\n \nAwareness and engagement activities on MyGov portal \nintroducing \nPMFBY \nQuiz and Crop Insurance Pledge\n.\n \n \nThe Crop Insurance week saw media coverage in close to 230 editions of national \nand regional newspapers and their e\n-\nversions, with state published Print Ads and \ncoverage stories in respective regional newspapers.   The campaign also received \na massive 326.\n61 million impression on its dedicated hashtags \n#CropInsuranceWeek, #PMFBYWeek on social media. \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n \nList of blocks/tehsils/revenue circles identified for \nfocussed \n \ncampaign during \nthe \nWeek\n \n(1st July \n-\n \n7th July 2021)\n \nin 75\n \nCrop Insurance\n \nAspirational/Tribal \nDistricts\n \n \nState\n \nSr. \nNo.\n \nDistrict\n \nLevel\n \nLevel Name\n \nCategory\n \nAndaman & \nNicobar \nIslands\n \n1\n \nSouth \nAndaman\n \nBlock\n \nFerrargunj\n \nLow enrolment\n \nAssam\n \n2\n \nBaksa\n \nCircle\n \nPathorighat \n(Pt)\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n3\n \nBarpeta\n \nCircle\n \nBarnagar \n(Pt)\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n4\n \nDarrang\n \nCircle\n \nSipajhar\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n5\n \nDhubri\n \nCircle\n \nChapar (Pt)\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n6\n \nGoalpara\n \nCircle\n \nDudhnai\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n7\n \nHailakandi\n \nCircle\n \nKatlichara\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n8\n \nUdalguri\n \nCircle\n \nMazbat\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n9\n \nBastar\n \nCircle\n \nFrejarpur\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n10\n \nKoriya\n \nCircle\n \nMansukh\n \nSuggested by \nState Govt.\n \n11\n \nDantewada\n \nCircle\n \nKirandul\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n12\n \nDurg\n \nCircle\n \nJunwani\n \nSuggested by \nState Govt.\n \n13\n \nKanker\n \nCircle\n \nBaande\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n14\n \nKondagaon\n \nCircle\n \nMardapal\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n15\n \nKorba\n \nCircle\n \nLafa\n \nAspirational with \n\nList of blocks/tehsils/revenue circles identified for \nfocussed \n \ncampaign during \nthe \nWeek\n \n(1st July \n-\n \n7th July 2021)\n \nin 75\n \nCrop Insurance\n \nAspirational/Tribal \nDistricts\n \n \nState\n \nSr. \nNo.\n \nDistrict\n \nLevel\n \nLevel Name\n \nCategory\n \nlow \nenrolment\n \n16\n \nMahasamund\n \nCircle\n \nMahasamund\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n17\n \nSurguja\n \nCircle\n \nPetla\n \nSuggested by \nState Govt.\n \n18\n \nNarayanpur\n \nCircle\n \nDhodhai\n \nAspirational with \nlow enrolment\n \n19\n \nRajnandagaon\n \nCircle\n \nRajnandgaon\n \nAspirational with \nlow \nenrolment\n \n20\n \nJashpur\n \nCircle\n \nAara\n \nSuggested by \nState Govt.\n \nGoa\n \n21\n \nSouth Goa\n \nBlock\n \nDharbandora\n \nLow enrolment\n \nJammu & \nKashmir\n \n22\n \nAnantnag