    "ls|LS17_S6_U_286": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 286 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 20TH JULY, 2021/ ASHADHA 29,1943 (SAKA) \n \nACCESS TO CCTNS \n \n286.  DR. SHASHI THAROOR: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has decided to allow  private companies to \nhave access to the Crime and  Criminals Tracking Network Systems \n(CCTNS) and other  Government databases for conducting background  \nchecks; \n \n(b) if so, whether all companies has been allowed to access the CCTNS; \n \n(c) whether the Government will allow this access to  those companies \nwho pay for this information; \n \n(d) if so, the details of the payment required and the  criteria used to \ndetermine the same; and \n \n(e) the safeguards that will be put in place to protect  the data of citizens \nand prevent its misuse in the hands  of private entities by the \nGovernment? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI AJAY KUMAR MISHRA) \n \n(a) No, Sir. \n(b) to (e) Does not arise in view of reply to part (a). \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_287": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *287 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 09.08.2021 \n  \nPMKVY IN TAMIL NADU \n \n*287.   DR. T.R. PAARIVENDHAR:  \n  \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n  \n(a)  the total number of youths, male and female se parately, who have been enrolled \nfrom Tamil Nadu for skill development training unde r the Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas \nYojana (PMKVY) during the last three years; \n \n(b)  the number of youths in the State, male and fe male separately, who have got \nemployment or placement after the training during the last three years; \n \n(c)  the total amount allotted and spent for this p rogramme during the last three years; \n \n(d) whether the Union Government proposes to set up  Skill Development Training \nCentres in the backward district of Perambalur in Tamil Nadu; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reas ons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER  \n  \nMINISTER OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) to (E) of LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *287 TO BE ANSWERED ON 09.08.2 021 ASKED BY DR. \nT.R. PAARIVENDHAR REGARDING ‘PMKVY IN TAMIL NADU’ \n \n(a) Under the Skill India Mission, Ministry of Skil l Development and Entrepreneurship \n(MSDE) is implementing its flagship scheme, Pradhan  Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana \n(PMKVY). Under PMKVY, in the last three years (2018 -21), 1.83 lakh female candidates \nand 1.88 lakh male candidates have been enrolled in the State of Tamil Nadu. \n \n  \n(b)       PMKVY has two training components, namely , Short-Term Training (STT) and \nRecognition of Prior Learning (RPL). STT is linked to placement, while RPL does not \nmandate placements as it recognizes the existing skills of candidates. Under STT-PMKVY, \nin the last three years (2018-21),  1.22 lakh (0.94  lakh female and 0.28 male) candidates \nhave been, as on 10.07.2021, certified in the State  of Tamil Nadu; out of which 0.82 lakh \n(0.63 lakh female and 0.19 male) candidates have been placed.  \n  \n(c)        Under PMKVY, during the last three years  (2018-21), the total budgetary allocation \nwas Rs. 5,230.05 crore; out of which, Rs. 5,037.19 crore was disbursed to implementing \nagencies, i.e., the National Skill Development Corp oration (NSDC) for Central component, \nand State Skill Development Mission (SSDM) / State Governments for the State \ncomponent for the implementation of the PMKVY acros s the country including the State of \nTamil Nadu.  \n  \n               Out of total disbursed funds in last  three years (2018-21) under PMKVY, Rs. \n172.43 crore (Rs. 138 crore under Central Component  and Rs. 34.43 crore under State \nComponent) was disbursed for the implementation of the scheme in the State of Tamil \nNadu.  \n  \n(d)       Ministry promotes establishment of model and aspirational skill centre known as \nPradhan Mantri Kaushal Kendra (PMKK) for imparting skill training in every district of the \ncountry, including  the district of Perambalur in t he State of Tamil Nadu. Ministry through \nNSDC provides funding support upto 75% of the proje ct investment for establishment of a \nPMKK in a district.  \n  \n               Also, under STT-PMKVY, training cent res (TCs) are empanelled for imparting \nshort duration training across the country, includi ng the district of Perambalur in the State \nof Tamil Nadu. Under RPL-PMKVY, candidates are oriented in camps, employer premises, \nPMKKs and large/medium enterprises.  \n  \n(e)               Till now, in the State of Tamil N adu, 35 PMKKs have been established, \nincluding 1 PMKK in the district of Perambalur. Als o, under STT-PMKVY, 2,325 TCs have \nbeen empanelled in the State of Tamil Nadu, includi ng 27 TCs in the district of \nPerambalur.  \n  \n******  ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_288": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 288 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nSCHEMES UNDER DISHA COMMITTEE \n \n288.  SHRI SUNIL BABURAO MENDHE: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the number of schemes and programmes of the Go vernment covered by District \nDevelopment Coordination and Monitoring Committee (DISHA); \n(b)  whether coordination between the State Governm ent and Central Government has been \nenvisaged as designed in DISHA so that resources are used optimally especially with \nrespect to the central sponsored schemes, if so, the details thereof; and \n(c)  the details of the outcomes achieved so far es pecially in the State of Maharashtra?  \n  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a) District DevelopmentCoordination and Monitoring Com mittee (DISHA) covers all non-statutory \nschemes of Government of India. However, at present , data of 43 Schemes/Programmesis made available \non DISHA Dashboard  and the list of these 43 Schemes are at Annexure .  \n(b) Yes, Sir. DISHA Committees have been formed to ensure better coordination through review \nand  monitoring of the non-statutory central scheme s to ensure theirefficient and time bound \nimplementation. For this purpose,these Committees have been formed under the Chairpersonship \nof Hon’ble Members of Parliament and also include e lected representatives at all levels and \noffice bearers concerned.The constitution  of DISHA   Committees at the State level,display of \ndata of different schemes at different levels on  D ISHA Dashboard etc. are  additional steps for \nthis end.  \n \n(c) In Maharashtra, District Level DISHA Committees hav e been formed in 36 Districts.So far,176 \nmeetings of District Level DISHA Committees have be en reported by State of Maharashtra.  The year -\nwise details are as under:  \n \nYear Number of Meetings \n2016-17 55 \n2017-18 54 \n2018-19 29 \n2019-20 18 \n2020-21 20 \n \n******* \n\nAnnexure \n \nAnnexure referred to into part (a) of the reply to the Lok Sabha USQ No. 288 for reply on \n20.07.2021 \n \n \nSchemes included for monitoring by DISHA Committee \nName of Ministry/Department Name of Program/Scheme \n1. Department of Rural \nDevelopment \n1. Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act \n(MGNREGA) \n2. DeenDayalAntyodaya Yojana – National Rural Livelihoods \nMission \n3. DeenDayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushalya Yojana – \nDDUGKY \n4. Pradhan Mantri Gram SadakYojana – PMGSY \n5. National Social Assistance  Programme – NSAP \n6. Pradhan MantriGraminAwasYojana – PMAY (G) \n7. National Rurban Mission –NruM \n2. Department  of Drinking \nWater and Sanitation \n8. Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) – SBM (G) \n9. National Rural Drinking Water Program – NRDWP \n3. Department of Land & \nResources \n10. Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sichayee Yojana - Integrated \nWatershed Mgmt Program –PMKSY –IWMP \n11. Digital India Land Record ModernisationPgm: DILRMP \n4. Ministry of Power 12.  Integrated Power Dev Scheme – IPDS \n13. DeenDayal Upadhyaya Gramin Jyoti Yojana- DDUGJY \n5. Ministry of Housing and \nUrban Affairs \n14. National Heritage City Dev& Augmentation Yojana - \nHRIDAY  \n15. Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation – \nAMRUT \n16. Pradhan Mantri AwasYojana (Urban)– PMAY (U) \n17. Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) – SBM (U) \n18. Smart City Mission \n6. Department of Agriculture 19.  Rashitrya Krishi Vikas Yojana – RKVY \n20. Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana – PKVY \n21. Soil Health Card – SHC \n22. Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sichayee Yojana : PMKSY \n23. National Agricultural Marker: E-NAM \n24. PMFBY –FasalBima Yojana \n7. Ministry of Health and \nFamily Welfare  \n25. National Health Mission – NHM \n8. Ministry of Human \nResource Development \n26. SarvaSiksha Abhiyan– SSA \n27. Mid-Day Meal Scheme \n9. Ministry 