    "ls|LS17_S6_U_324": "O.I.H.  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 324 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nNATIONAL RURAL LIVELIHOOD MISSION \n \n324.  SHRI JASWANT SINGH BHABHOR: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the main objective of the National Rural Livel ihood Mission; \n(b)  the number of people of Gujarat State likely t o be covered under this scheme; and \n(c)  whether the scheme will be implemented in the tribal areas of Gujarat also and if so, the \ndetails thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a) Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana – National Rural Liv elihoods Mission (DAY-NRLM) is \nbeing implemented since 2011 in a mission mode with  the objective of organizing the \nrural poor women into Self Help Groups (SHGs), and continuously nurturing and \nsupporting them to take economic activities till th ey attain appreciable increase in \nincome over a period of time to improve their quali ty of life and come out of abject \npoverty. The programme aims to ensure that at least  one woman member from each \nrural poor household (about 9-10 crore) is brought into women SHGs and their \nfederations within a definite time frame. The progr amme is being implemented in all the \nStates and Union Territories, except Delhi and Chandigarh.  \n \n(b) In Gujarat, about 36.53 lakh rural households a re likely to be covered under DAY-\nNRLM by the financial year 2023-24. The identificat ion of households is based on the \nSocio Economic Caste Census (SECC) (deprived and au to-included households) data \nand households identified through the process of Pa rticipatory Identification of Poor \n(PIP). Gujarat State has mobilized 26.03 lakh rural  households under the Scheme till \n30 th  June 2021, i.e. 71% of the total targeted households. \n \n(c) DAY-NRLM is being implemented in all 248 blocks  of 33 districts that includes tribal \nareas of Gujarat. As on 30 th  June 2021, a total of 7,67,625 women from Schedule d Tribe \n(ST) households are mobilised into 73,191 Self Help Groups (SHGs). \n \n******* \n  ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_325": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 325 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nANNAPURNA SCHEME \n \n325.  SHRI MAHESH SAHOO: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware about the non release of central allocation of rice and \nfunds under Annapurna Scheme to Odisha during the F Y 2019-20 which have been \ndistributed to the beneficiaries from the State pool; and \n(b)  the time which the Government would release th e central allocation of rice and fund to \nOdisha under the scheme during the FY 2019-20 and FY 2020-21?  \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n  \n \n(a)  & (b)  During 2019-20, the Ministry of Consumer Af fairs, Food and Public Distribution has \nallocated 3888.00 MT of rice to the State of Odisha  under Annapurna Scheme. An amount of \nRs.552.61 lakh has been released to the State under  this Scheme during the financial year 2019-\n20.  The State of Odisha has been requested to subm it the revised food grain Utilization \nCertificates in the prescribed format for allocatio n of food grains and release of funds for the \nyears 2019-20 and 2020-21.   \n \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_326": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 326 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20th JULY, 2021 \n \nBio-Toilets on Fishing Vessels \n \n326. DR. BEESETTI VENKATA SATYAVATHI: \n SHRI SANJAY KAKA PATIL: \n \n Will the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING \nमत्स्यपाऱन, पशुपाऱन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government has mandated the fishing vessels to shift to bio -toilets to \nensure marine environment clean and contamination of marine resources is prevented;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  whether any financial assistance is being provided to vessel owners to install bio -\ntoilets; and  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof? \n \n ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY DAIRYING \n \n(Dr. L. MURUGAN) \n \n(a) to (d) : The endeavor of Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal \nHusbandry and Dairying, Government of India is to promote environment friendly marine \nfishing practices among the fishers. The installation of bio -toilets on mechanical fishing \nvessels is one such activity. Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal \nHusbandry and Dairying, Government of India under the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada \nYojana (PMMSY) provides financial support for fitment of Bio toilets in mechanized fishing \nvessels for maintaining hygiene, prevention and spread of diseases, prevention of pollution of \noceans and seas and protection  of their ecology.   Under the PMMSY, the Department of \nFisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying , during the financial year \n2020-21, accorded approval to the proposals of seven States/UTs namely Andaman and \nNicobar Islands, Andhra Pradesh, Goa, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Odisha and Puducherry for \nfitment of 2755 Bio-toilets in mechanized fishing vessels at a total cost Rs.1377.50 lakh with \na central assistance of Rs. 395.24 lakh.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_327": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO: 327 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20TH JULY, 2021 \n \nPREVENTION OF CRUELTY TO ANIMALS ACT, 1960 \n \n327. SHRI KUMBAKUDI SUDHAKARAN: \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMALHUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nमत्स्यपाऱन, पशुपाऱन और डेयरी मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has received petitionsseeking amendment of ‘The  Prevention \nof Cruelty toAnimals Act, 1960’ (PCA Act), if so, the detailsthereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government agrees with the opinionthat the penalties prescribed in the PCA \nAct are minimaland do not act as a deterrent; \n \n(c) whether the Government is considering to amendPCA Act to inflation correct and revise \nthe prescribed penalities; \n \n(d) whether the Government is considering to amendSection 11(1) (a) to 11(1) (o) and \nsection 38 of the Actwhich recognises the cognizability of offences under theAct; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasonstherefor? \n  \n ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n(a)  Yes. Sir.  The Government has received large number of suggestions, petitions and requests \nfrom various sections of the societies to increase the existing penalties in the Prevention of Cruelty \nto Animal Act, 1960. \n(b) Yes. Sir. \n(c) to (e) The need for amending the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals Act, 1960 by introducing \nmore stringent penalties has been recognized by the Government. The draft amendment worked out \nincludes increasing monetary penalties and punishment provisions including amendment of Section \n11 and Section 38 of the Act. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_328": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 328 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 20TH JULY, 2021/ ASHADHA 29, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nMEDICAL OFFICERS IN PARA-MILITARY FORCES \n \n328.     ADV. A.M. ARIFF: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken any steps for recruiting to the posts \nof Specialist Medical Officers and  Medical Officers in Central Para -Military \nForces, namely,  Central Reserve Police Force, Border Security Force,  \nAssam Rifles, Sashastra Seema Bal and Indo-Tibetan Border Police. \n \n(b) if so, the details of the un -filled vacancies in the  above category as on \n15th February 2021 force-wise; and \n \n(c) whether the Government will take any steps to  expedite the \nrecruitment process by appointing candidates  from reserve rank list of \ncandidates before its expiry? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI)  \n(a) & (b):  Recruitment of Specialist and General Duty Medical Officers in \nCentral Armed Police Forces & Assam Rifles is being made regularly \nthrough Medical Officers Selection Board (MOSB).  \n \nThe force -wise details of the un -filled vacancies of Specialist Medical \nOfficers (Spl. MO) and General Duty Medical Officers (GDMOs) as on 15th \nFebruary, 2021 is as under:- \n \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.328 FOR 20.07.2021 \n \n \nForce Spl.MOs GDMOs \nAR 04 31 \nBSF 51 93 \nCRPF 112 85 \nITBP* 08 70 \nSSB 18 53 \n*ITBP Cadre includes Medical Officers of CISF also.  \n \nFurther, in the wake of Covid -19 pandemic, CRPF has been allowed to \nrecruit General Duty Medical Officers (GDMOs) on contract basis against \nvacant posts of Specialists Medical Officers for a period of one year. \n \n(c): Offers have already been given to the candidates in the reserve list of \nlast MOSB and many candidates have joined against the vacant posts. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_329": "O.I.H.  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 329 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nALLOCATION OF BUDGET UNDER MGNREGS \n \n329.  SHRI HANUMAN BENIWAL: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the budget allocated to Rajasthan by the Union  Government and utilization thereof under \nMahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) during \n2019-20, 2020-21 and till June, 2021 of the current financial year, the details thereof, \nitem wise; and \n(b)  the amount which remained unspent by the Rajas than Government out of the total budget \nallocated under MGNREGS during the aforesaid period and the reasons therefor for the \nsame?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a):    The Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employmen t Guarantee Scheme (Mahatma Gandhi \nNREGS) is a demand driven wage employment programme  which provide for the enhancement \nof livelihood security of the households in rural a reas of the country by providing at least one \nhundred days of guaranteed wage employment in every financial year to every household whose \nadult members volunteer to do unskilled manual work . Being a demand driven programme, no \nState/UT-wise (including State of Rajasthan) financial allocation is made.  \n \n The details of funds released by Central Governmen t to the State of Rajasthan for the \nimplementation of Mahatma Gandhi NREG Scheme during  the last two financial years 2019-\n20, 2020-21 and the current FY 2021-22 (as on 30.06.2021) is given below: \n(Rs. In crore) \nIndicators 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 \nCentral funds released 6891.74 9129.02 3271.79 \n \n(b):        As per information provided by State Go vernment of Rajasthan, the unspent balance \nwith State was Rs.1186.46 crore as on 31.03.2020 at  the end of financial year 2019-20, and an \namount of Rs. 214.87 crore was remaining unspent as on 31.03.2021 at the end of FY 2020-21.  \n \n******  ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_330": "1\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULT\nURE AND FARMERS WELF\nARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICU\nLTURE, COOPERATION A\nND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n330\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n20\nTH\n \nJULY\n, 2021\n \nSMALL AND MARGINAL F\nARMERS\n \n \n330\n. \nDR. ALOK KUMAR SUMAN\n \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to \nState:\n \n(a) \n \nW\nhether it is fact that the Government has initiated any specific programme to help \nsmall and marginal farmers in the country including district Gopalganj of Bihar; \n \n(b) \n \nI\nf so, the number of such farmers covered under such schemes in the last two years, \nSt\nate and year\n-\nwise; and \n \n(c) \n \nT\nhe details of measures taken to mitigate the sufferings of small and marginal farmers \nin the country including Gopalganj district of Bihar?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE \nAND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nक ृ िष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n   \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH\n \nTOMAR)\n \n(\na\n)\n \nMost Schemes\n \nie Central Sector and Centrally Sponsored,\n \nof the\n \nDepart\nment of \nAgriculture\n \nand Farmers Welfare \n(DA\n&FW) are for the benefit of small and\n \nmarginal \nfarmers in the country\n,\n \nincluding district Gopalganj of Bihar\n. \n \n(\nb\n)\n \nBeneficiaries \nof these schemes\n, specially Centrally Sponsored Schemes,\n \nare decided/ \nselected by the respective State Governments and therefore\n \ndetails are available with \nthem\n. However, Data on central sector schemes like PM\n-\nKISAN, Pradhan Mantri Kisan \nMaandhan Yojana (PM\n-\nKMY) and Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana \n(PMFBY) are \ngiven in the Annexure\n \nI\n.\n \n(\nc\n)\n \nAllocation and release in respect of major Centrally Sponsored Schemes in the c\nountry \nincluding for the State of Bihar is attached as Annexure II \n \n \n\n2\n \n