    "ls|LS17_S6_U_331": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRYAND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF FISHERIES \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 331 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20TH JULY, 2021 \n \nEffect of COVID-19 Pandemic on the Fishing Sector \n \n331.  ADV. ADOOR PRAKASH: \n  \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  मत्स्यपाऱन, \nपशुपाऱन और डेयरी मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware that the fishing sector in the country is facing deep crisis after \nthe spread of COVID-19 pandemic; \n \n(b)  whether the Government has assessed the situation and taken any supportive measures for the \nstruggling fishermen and lakhs of people dependent on this sector for their livelihood, if so, the \ndetails thereof; and \n \n(c)  whether the Government will consider a special scheme for compensating the job loss among \nfishermen, if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRYAND DAIRYING \n(Dr. L MURUGAN) \n(a) to (c):  The Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, with a \nview to avoid adverse impact on fisheries due to COVID -19 pandemic lockdown in the country, had \nissued advisory to State Governments/Union Territories(UTs) to include fish and shrimp in the list of \nexempted commodities during lockdown and also allow movement of fish and fish products, fish seed \n& fish feed for fish -farmers/fishers, aquaculture farms and other commercial establishments like \naquarium shop etc. Besides, the Guidelines issued on 10th April, 2020 by the Ministry of Home Affairs \nalso allowed operations of the fishing(marine)/aquaculture industry including feeding & maintenance, \nharvesting, processing, packaging, cold chain, sale and marketing, hatcheries, feed plants, commercial \naquaria, movement of fish/shrim p and fish products, seed/feed and workers , during the lockdown \nperiod.  \n Besides, the Department of Fisheries, Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying is \nimplementing a flagship scheme namely “Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) - to \nbring about Blue Revolution through sustainable and responsible development of fisheri es sector in \nIndia” with an estimated investment of Rs. 20,050 crore  for a period of 5 years  from financial year \n2020-21 to FY 2024 -25 in all States/Union Territories as a part of Aatma Nirbhar Bharat Package.  \nWhile enhancing fish production and productivi ty, PMMSY also aims to create huge employment \nopportunities both direct and indirect in fisheries and aquaculture sector. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_332": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 332  \nANSWERED ON 20.07.2021 \n  \nPANCHAYATI RAJ SYSTEM IN ASSAM \n \n 332.        SHRI ABDUL KHALEQUE: \nWill the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n(a)          The details of various schemes available under the Panchayati Raj system in the State \nof Assam particularly in the districts of Barpeta and Bongaigaon; and \n (b)         the total funds allocated during the last  five financial years and fund ut ilized so far, \nyear-wise the details thereof?     \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PANCHAYATI RAJ \n(SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL) \n \n(a) The Ministry of Panchayati Raj (M oPR) implements the Centrally Sponsored Scheme -\nRashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA) and Incentivisation of Panchayats (IoP) , a Central \ncomponent of RGSA in all States including the State of Assam and its districts of Barpeta and \nBonaigaon for Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) for strengthening the PRIs and incentivisation \nfor their developmental works.  \n \n(b) No prior allocation of funds is made to any States under the Schemes of Ministry of \nPanchayati Raj. The funds under the Scheme RGSA is released based on the annual action plan \nsubmitted by the State concerned including the State of Assam and funds under the scheme of \nIncentivisation of Panchyats is released to the best performing Panchayats selecte d through a \nnational competition for the National Panchayat Awards of various categories. A total of \nRs.172.17 crore  of grants -in-aid was released to the State of Assam under the two above \nschemes during the last five years, out of which Rs.1.54 crore remains unutilised. The year -\nwise releases under the two schemes is as under:   \n   \n Year Releases under RGSA \nScheme (Rs. in crore) \n   Releases under IoP Scheme \n(Rs. in crore) \n2016-17* 49.08 1.72 \n2017-18* 27.59 1.37 \n2018-19 39.21 1.30 \n2019-20 23.22 0.97 \n2020-21 26.12 1.59 \nTotal 165.22 6.95 \n*Capacity Building-Panchayat Sashaktikaran Abhiyan (CB-PSA) \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_333": "O.I.H\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n333\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n20\nTH\n \nJULY\n, 2021\n \n \nIMPACT OF PANDEMIC ON DIRECT AGRICULTURAL\n \nMARKETING\n \n333\n.  \nSHRI CHUNNI LAL SAHU:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS\n \n \nWELFARE   \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether direct agricultural marketing was\n \nadversely affected during the \n \nlockdown period in the\n \nyear \n2020 due to the COVID\n-\n19 pandemic;\n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; and\n \n \n(c) \n \nthe details of the number of farmers linked to the\n \nKisan Rath Mobile app so far \n \nand the number of farmers\n \nbenefited, State\n-\nwise?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS\n \nWELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH\n \nTOMAR)\n \n \n(a) & (b): \n \nNo Sir.  In view of the above, the question does not arise. \n \n(c):\n \n \nA \ntotal of 4,85,103 farmers are registered on the Kisan Rath Mobile \nApplication. A farmer linked to Kisan \nRath may benefit through various options \navailable on the app such as posting load, receiving response against these loads, \nviewing partial loads nearby, viewing service providers nearby.\n \n \nHowever, t\nhe state\n-\nwise status of registration of farmers on Kisan \nrath\n \nat Annexure\n-\nI.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \nS.No.\n \nStates/Uts\n \nNo. of Farmers registered on Kisan Rath\n \n1\n \nAnd\na\nman and Nicobar Island\n \n21\n \n2\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n18728\n \n3\n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n224\n \n4\n \nAssam\n \n19060\n \n5\n \nBihar\n \n36811\n \n6\n \nChandigarh\n \n42\n \n7\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n8066\n \n8\n \nDadra\n \nand Nagar Haveli and\n \