    "ls|LS17_S6_U_339": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 339 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nPMGSY IN TAMIL NADU \n \n339.  SHRI S. VENKATESAN: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the number of colonies connected so far under Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana \n(PMGSY) in the country, along with the district-wise details in respect of Tamil Nadu \nincluding Madurai; and \n(b)  the number of roads identified under PMGSY dur ing the said period?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n \n(a)& (b) Rural Roads is a State subject. Pradhan Ma ntri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) \nwas launched as a one-time special intervention to support enhancement of rural connectivity, by \nway of a single all-weather road, to the eligible unconnected habitations of designated population \nsize (500+ in plain areas and 250+ in North-Eastern  States, Himalayan States and Himalayan \nUnion Territories as per 2001 census) in the core n etwork for uplifting the socio-economic \ncondition of the rural population. Relaxation has b een provided to the Tribal (Schedule V) areas \nand Selected Tribal and Backward Districts (as iden tified by the Ministry of Home Affairs \n(MHA) and Planning Commission), and unconnected habitations in these areas with a population \nof 250 persons and above in the Core Network as per  Census 2001 are eligible for connectivity \nunder the scheme. In the critical Left Wing Extremi sm affected blocks (as identified by Ministry \nof Home Affairs), additional relaxation has been gi ven to connect habitations with population \n100 persons and above as per 2001 census.   \n        \nThe unit for PMGSY programme is habitation. Against  1,78,184 habitations of the population \nsize 250+ and 500+ identified for coverage under PM GSY, 16,086 habitations have been \nprovided connectivity by the States/UTs out of thei r own resources and 4,716  habitations have \neither been dropped or have not been found feasible . Out of the balance 1,57,382  habitations \nsanctioned for providing connectivity under the PMG SY, 1,55,245 habitations have already been \nprovided connectivity. In the State of Tamilnadu, 1 ,985 habitations of 500+ and 1,000+ \npopulation size were sanctioned for coverage under PMGSY and all the habitations have already \nbeen connected. The district-wise details of habita tions sanctioned and connected in the State of \nTamilnadu, including Madurai are attached as Annexure . \n \nThe mandate of PMGSY has been subsequently widened to include new interventions.  PMGSY-\nII was launched in the year 2013, with a target to upgrade 50,000 Kms  of the existing rural road \nnetwork to improve its overall efficiency as a prov ider of transportation services for people, \ngoods and services.  Road Connectivity Project for Left Wing Extremism Affected Areas \n(RCPLWEA) was launched in the year 2016 for constru ction/upgradation of strategically \n\nimportant roads chosen in the 44 worst affected LWE  districts and adjoining districts in the 9 \nStates of Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Chhattisgarh, Jhar khand, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, \nOdisha, Telangana and Uttar Pradesh. PMGSY-III was launched in the year 2019 for \nconsolidation of 1,25,000 Km Through Routes and Maj or Rural Links connecting \nhabitations,  inter-alia, to Gramin Agricultural Markets (GrAMs), Higher Secondary Schools and \nHospitals.   \n \nThe status of implementation of various interventio ns/verticals of PMGSY across the country \nand in the Tamilnadu State and Madurai district as on 15 \nth  July, 2021 is as under:- \n \nOverall status in the country \n \nRoad length in Km \nName of intervention  Sanctioned Completed Balance* \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nPMGSY-I 1,64,816  6,45,644  1,58,305  6,07,871  6,511  22,710  \nPMGSY-II 6,708  49,904  5,206  44,340  1,502  5,124  \nRCPLWEA** 894  9,268  190  4,126  704  5,123  \nPMGSY-III 8,089  62,968  302  13,644  7,787  49,318  \nTotal 1,80,507  7,67,784  1,64,003  6,69,981  16,504  82,275  \n \nTamilnadu State \n \nRoad length in Km \nName of intervention  Sanctioned Completed Balance* \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nPMGSY-I 7,678  16,320  7,668  16,151  10  18  \nPMGSY-II 860  2,940  852  2,934  08  04  \nPMGSY-III 880  3,198  99  660  781  2,538  \nTotal 9,418  22,458  8,619  19,745  799  2,560  \n \n \nMadurai district  \nRoad length in Km \nName of intervention  Sanctioned Completed Balance* \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nNumber \nof roads \nRoad \nlength \nPMGSY-I 280  512  280  512  0 0 \nPMGSY-II 36  126  36  126  0 0 \nPMGSY-III 13  42  02  06  11  35  \nTotal 329  680  318  644  11  35  \n \n*Balance road length may be less than the difference  of sanctioned and completed length due to \nvarious reasons such as reduction in curve length, change in alignment, construction of part \nlength by other agencies, etc. \n \n** Does not pertain to Tamilnadu. \n \n****** \n  \n\nAnnexure  \n \nAnnexure referred to in part (a)  of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No.339 for 20 th  July, \n2021  \nDistrict-wise details of sanctioned and  connected habitations in Tamil Nadu  \n \nSl. No Name of district \nTotal sanctioned \nHabitations \nTotal Connected \nHabitations \n1 Ariyalur 26  26  \n2 Coimbatore 39  39  \n3 Cuddalore 49  49  \n4 Dharmapuri 33  33  \n5 Dindigul 77  77  \n6 Erode 53  53  \n7 Kanchipuram 23  23  \n8 Kanniyakumari 62  62  \n9 Karur 36  36  \n10 Krishnagiri 33  33  \n11 Madurai 73  73  \n12 Nagapattinam 110  110  \n13 Namakkal 12  12  \n14 Perambalur 11  11  \n15 Pudukkottai 84  84  \n16 Ramanathapuram 119  119  \n17 Salem 51  51  \n18 Sivagangai 58  58  \n19 Thanjavur 93  93  \n20 The Nil