-Gramin (PMAY-G):   \n \nSince funds under Rural Housing Scheme are being released directly to the State Governments \nfrom the year 2014-15 and district wise releases we re not made. However, as reported by \nStates on Awaassoft as on 13.07.2021 the utilizatio n/fund spent in respect of Jhunjhunu, \nChuru, Alwar, and Sikar districts of Rajasthan and Latur district of Maharashtra  is given \nbelow: \n(Rs. in crore) \nRajasthan \nFinancial year* Jhunjhunu Churu Alwar Sikar \n2016-17 0.927 0.33 1.8150 1.083 \n2017-18 8.44 55.96 34.87 14.6022 \n2018-19 2.67 105.30 27.44 12.0558 \n2019-20 3.00 47.92 20.13 8.3178 \n2020-21 0.92 49.05 8.89 3.8145 \n2021-22 0.0165 6.42 0.31 0.1425 \n                    \n                        (Rs. in crore) \nMaharashtra \nFinancial year* Latur \n2016-17 6.339 \n2017-18 33.73 \n2018-19 2.18 \n2019-20 9.44 \n2020-21 1.65 \n2021-22 0.12 \n* PMAY-G started from 2016. \nSource:B3 report of Awaasssoft reported by States/UTs as on 15.07.2021 \n \n \n\n \n(v)  Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY ) \n \nThe details of amount allocated/ released in the di strict of Sikar, Jhunjhunu, Churu and Alwar of \nRajasthan and Latur district of Maharashtra from th e years 2014 and 2019 till date and also the \ndetails of works undertaken under PMGSY on the abov e districts are available at \nwww.omms.nic.in → Proposals →State wise list of Roa ds. \n  \n (vi) Shyama Prasad Mukherjee Rurban Mission (SPMRM):    \n \nOnly Alwar district in Rajasthan has one cluster Na ugawan whereas no any Rurban cluster fall \nunder the Latur district of Maharashtra. The Critic al Gap Fund of Rs. 8.10 Crore released to the \nState Government for  Naugawan cluster as Central s hare and the corresponding State share is \nRs. 5.40 Crore. The Naugawan cluster has made the t otal expenditure of Rs. 9.04 Crore since \nMission’s implantation. \n \n(vii)  National Social Assistance Programme (NSAP): \n \nThe district-wise fund allocation and utilization is not maintained under NSAP. Data with respect \nto state of Rajasthan and Maharashtra is given as Annexure-I.  \n \n*******  ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_392": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRYoFcoNsUf{tERAFFA|RS,FooD&PUBLIGDISTRIBUTIoN\nDEPARTIVIENT OF FOOD AND PUBLTC DISTRIBUTION\nDUTY ON GRUDE PALM OIL\n392. SHRI BHOLASINGH:\nSHRI MANOJ KOTAK:\nSHRI RAJVEER SINGH (RAJU BHAIYA):\nSHRI RAJA AMARESHWARA NAIK:\nSHRI NARANBHAI KACHHADIYA:\nSHRI PARBATBHAI SAVABHAI PATEL:\nSHRI VINOD KUMAR SONKAR:\nWill the Minister of GONSUMER AFFAIRST FOOD AND PUBLIG\nDISTRTBUTTOX sEre{ttrr arri, uru glk Urffio fud{q uifr be pteased to state!\n(a) whether the Government has reduced duty on crude palm oil by 5\npercent to reduce edible oil prices to bring relaef to the consumels;\n(b) if so, the detaits thereof and its impact on prices;\n(c) whether the Govemment has recommended removal of the restriction\non:mportofRBDPalmotein(RefinedPalmoil)andtoputitintheopen\ngeneral category of imports, if so, the details thereof along wath the total\ndomestic demand for edible oils in the country;\n(d) the measures being taken by the Ministry to enhance the production\nof refined oil in the eountry especially in Guiarat; and\n(e) whether the Govemment has stressed on creation of modern storage\nfacilities at grass root and btock levels for essential commodities to\nincrease farmers! incomer if sor the action taken thereon?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MIilISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT AND\nCONSUMER AFFAIRS' FOOD & PUBLIG DISTRIBUTIOI{\n(SADHVI NIRAilJAN JYOTI)\n(a) & (b): Yes' Sir. The Government vide Notification No. 34/202{ -Customsr dated\nde palm oil bY 529th Juner 2O21, has reduced the standard rate of duty on cru\npercent from 30.06.2O2{ and will effect upto 30th September' 2O2{'\n......2t-\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 392\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2O11{JULY,2O21\n\n.2-\n(c): The Goyernment vide DGFTts Notification No. { O/2O15'2O2O dated 3Oh\nJune, 202{, has amended the import Poticy of Refined Palm Oils from\nsrestrictedt to \"freet with immediate effect and for a period of upto\n31.12.2021. The domestac production of edible oils in the country is unable\nto meet the domestic demand of around 25O LMT and the Gountry has to\nrely on imports to meet the sholtfall.\n(d): To enhance the production of refined oil in the country, the standard\nrate of duty on crude palm oil has been reduced lo lOo/o from 30.O6.202{\nand will effect upto 30th Septembeq2O2l.\n(e): Storage capaclty of FCI depends upon the level of\nprocurement, requirement of buffer norms and PDS. Storage gap ls\nassessed in the procurlng states based on the highest stock levels in the\nlast three years and in the consuming states on the basis of 4 months (6\nmonths in case of l{E regions) requirement of NFSA and OWS.\nFGI is augmenting lts storage capacity through following schemes :'\n{. Private Entrepreneurs Guarantee (PEG) Scheme\n2. Gentre Sector Scheme (GSS).\n3. Gonstruction of SILO's under PPP mode\n4. Hiring of godown from GWGs/SWGs/State Agencies\n5. Private Warehousing Scheme (PWS)\nAs on 3O.O6.2O2tr Storage capacity available with FGI and State\nagencies for storage of central poot foodgEin stock is 9{5.65 Lakh MT\n(Govered -723.4 LMT and GAP - {93.21 LMT).\nGWG has floated Eol for settang up cold storage in its warchousos on\nPAN tndia basls. GWG lntends to develop cold Ghaln facilitles at\naround .l9o locatlons. Gwc has slgned MoU with ilAFED for provldlng\nstorage space and related services by cwc to NAFED for the procurement\noperation to be undertaken by I{AFED.\n.....3/-\nThe domestic wholesale and retail prices as on 13.7.2021 on\ncomparison with the prlces on 29.o,fi..2021 is given below:\n(i) The wholesale prices of groundnut oil, mustard oil, vanaspatar RBD\npatmoleln and sesame oil increased by 1-82o/o1 0.610/o1 0.67o/o1 O.360/o and\nO.837o respectivety while the prices of soyabean oil, sunflower oll and\ncoconut oil decreased by O.34\"/\"1O.3{% and 3.9{o/o respectively.\n(ii) The retait prices of groundnut oit, mustard oil, Yanaspati, soyabean oil\nand RBD palmolein increased by {.OO%, O.7Oo/o1 1.54o/o2 O.23o/o and 0.64o/o\nrespectively while the prices of sunflower oil decreased by O.13%.\n\n-3-\nA new model for c/o storage in remote areas has been implemented\nunder which MOU has been slgned between GWG and FGI for clo\ngodowns on FGI land by CWC on guaranteed hiring basis in Zanskar &\nDrass, Ladakh (3340 MT each) & Zunheboto , Nagaland (5OOO MT) &\namsai ({670 MT} Arunachal\nMOU has been signed on 19.O3.2O2{ with Arunachal Agricultural\nMarketing Board for setting up Farm Gate Logistics lnfrastructure @\nRs.{.8Ocr./5O:5O profit sharing basis in 3 districts'Lower Subansiri,\nGhanglang & Lohit.",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_393": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 393 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nHARVESTING UNDER MGNREGS \n \n393.  SHRI Y. DEVENDRAPPA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is considering to bring pre-sowing and post-harvest activities \nunder Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guar antee Scheme(MGNREGS); \nand \n(b)  if so, the details of concrete proposal made o r funds earmarked for the same? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a)  & (b)   Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment G uarantee Scheme (Mahatma Gandhi \nNREGS) is a demand driven wage employment programme  which provide for the enhancement \nof livelihood security of the households in rural a reas of the country by providing at least one \nhundred days of guaranteed wage employment in every  financial year to every household whose \nadult members volunteer to do unskilled manual work.  \nGram Panchayat is the implementing agency under the  Mahatma Gandhi National Rural \nEmployment Guarantee Scheme at Panchayat level and at least 50 percent of the works are to be \nimplemented by Gram Panchayats.  \n \nSub-para 3 of paragraph 4 of the Schedule -I of the  Mahatma Gandhi NREG Act provides as \nunder: “Works, which are non-tangible, not measurab le, repetitive such as removing grass, \npebbles, agricultural operations shall not be taken up.”  \n \nAccordingly, there is no proposal to bring pre-sowi ng and post-harvest activities under Mahatma \nGandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (Mahatma Gandhi NREGA). \n \nHowever, it needs to be mentioned that as per para 4 (2) of the Schedule - I of the Mahatma \nGandhi NREGA provides that “The District Programme Coordinator shall ensure th at at least \n60% of the works to be taken up in a district in te rms of cost shall be for creation of productive \nassets directly linked to agriculture and allied ac tivities through development of land, water and \ntrees.”  \n \nThus, implementation framework has been designed in  a manner which promotes \nagriculture and related activities. Under Mahatma Gandhi NREGA out of 262 permissible works, \n164 works relate to agri and allied activities. Mah atma Gandhi NREGA is a demand driven \nprogramme and the permissible works related to agri  and allied activities are taken up under the \nScheme, as per demand. \n   \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_394": " \nGOVERNEMNT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 394\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 20\nTH\n \nJULY,2021\n \n \nFUNCTIONING OF PM\n-\nKISAN SCHEME\n \n \n394. ADV. DEAN \nKURIAKOSE:\n \n        \nDR. NISHIKANT DUBEY:\n \n \nWill the Minister of Agr\niculture and Farmers Welfare\n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe quantum of funds disburesed, the number of beneficiaries identified under the \nPradhan Mantri Kisan \nSamman Nidhi Yojana (PM\n-\nKISAN) and the number of the \nbeneficiaries being benefited under the same till date;\n \n \n(b)\n \nthe number of beneficiaries identified in Jharkhand , especially Santhal Pargana, \nunder the PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme and the number of beneficiaries be\ning\n \nbenefited\n \nat \npresent;\n \n \n(c) \n \nthe names of the States where the PM\n-\nKISAN Scheme is not being implemented \nproperly and the reasons therefor;\n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether any payments to farmers are pending, if so, the details thereof; and \n \n \n(e) \n \nwhether\n \nthe Government intends to provide additional income support to farmers, \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a)\n:\n \nThe Pradhan Mantri\n \nKisan\n \nSamman\n \nNidhi (PM\n-\nKISAN) is a Central Sector \nScheme, being implemented since 1\nst\n \nDec\nember, 2018.  The Scheme aims to provide\n \nfinancial assistance to landholding farmer families across the country, subject to certain \nexclusion criteria, to enable them to take care \nof expenses related to agriculture and \nallied activities\n,\n \nas well as\n,\n \ndomestic needs.  Under the Scheme, an amount of Rs. \n6000/\n-\n \nper year is transferred in three 4\n-\nmonthly installments of Rs.2000/\n-\n \ndirectly into \nthe bank accounts of the farmers. \nOut of 11.\n93 registered farmers under the Scheme, \napproximately 11.08 crore beneficiaries have been \ngiven financial\n \nbenef\nits of more than \nRs. 1.37\n \nlakh\n \ncrore through various installments as on 14.07.2021.\n \n\n \n \n \n(b)\n:  \n \nIn State of Jharkhand, approximately 26.05 lakhs\n \nbeneficiaries have been given \nfinancial benefits of more than Rs. 2354.11/\n-\n \ncrore through various installments \nunder \nPM\n-\nKISAN Scheme. Also, more than 6.43 lakhs\n \nbeneficiaries are getting the benefits of \nPM\n-\nKISAN Scheme\n \nin the Santhal Pargana Division\n \nof J\nharkhand.\n \n(c)\n:  \n \nPM\n-\nKISAN Scheme is \nbeing succefully \nimplemented \nacross\n \nthe country. \n \n(d)\n:\n \nAs PM\n-\nKISAN is a continuous and ongoing Scheme under which benefit of the \nScheme is provided to eligible landholding farmers families as and when their correct \nand v\nerified data is received on PM\n-\nKISAN portal from the respective States/Uts and its \nvalidation through Aadhaar/PFMS and Income Tax database, the question does not \narise. \n \n(e)\n:\n \nThere is no such proposal under consideration at present. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n******\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_395": " \nORIGINAL IN HINDI \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution \nDepartment of Consumer Affairs \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 395 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 20.07.2021 \n \n \nGRAHAK SUVIDHA KENDRAS \n \n395. SHRI VIJAY BAGHEL: SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SONI: SHRI ARUN SAO:  \n(OIH) \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is contemplating on proposal regarding setting up Grahak Suvidha \nKendras in various cities of the country;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the details of the cities identified for setting - up the said Grahak Suvidha Kendras, S tate-wise/city-\nwise; and  \n(d)  the other efforts being made by the Government to make the customers/consumers aware of their \nrights? \n \nANSWER \n \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k jkT; ea=h  \n¼Jh vf”ouh dqekj pkScs½ \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY) \n \n (a) to  (c) : No, Sir \n  \n(d)     :  To make consumers aware of their rights, the Govt. has launched the “Jago Grahak Jago” \ncampaign through print, electronic, outdoor and social m edia for consumer awareness and advocacy of \nconsumer rights. Consumer awareness and education is also promoted by State Governments with Central \nassistance under the Consumer Welfare Fund. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_396": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 396\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n20\nTH\n \nJULY\n, 2021\n \n \nAssessment of Crop Damage due to Cyclone Yaas \n \n \n \n396\n.   SHRI \nNITESH GANGA DEB\n:     \n \n  \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE \nAND\n \nFARMERS WELFARE \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the central Government team has visited Odisha recently to assess the crop \ndamage due to cyclone Yaas\n \nin the affected districts\n;\n \n \n(b) \nif so\n, the details of the crop damage in these districts\n;\n \n \n(c) whether the Ministry has sanctioned any financial package to the farmers of the \naffected districts; and\n \n \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AG\nRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n     \n \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n(a) to\n \n(d\n): \n \nA\nn\n \nInter\n-\nMinisterial Central Team (IMCT)\n, constituted by the Ministry of \nHome Affairs,\n \nvisited Odisha\n \nin June 2021 for an on the spot assessment of damages in \nthe\n \nwake of Cyclone “Yaas” that struck\n \nOdisha in May 2021. \nAs per the Memorandum \nsubmitted by the State Government, \n2197.34 hectares of agriculture\n/\nhorticulture crops \nsustained\n \ncrop loss to the extent of 33% \nand above\n. \nAs per the existing procedure, the \nreport of the IMCT is considered by the Sub Committee of National Executive \nCommittee (SC\n-\nNEC). Thereafter, the High Level Committee (HLC) approves the final \nquantum of financial\n \nassistance.\n \n******\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_397": "O.I.H.   \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 397 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nPMAY(G) IN MAHARASHTRA \n \n397.  SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Gramin ) is functional in the State of \nMaharashtra; \n(b)  if so, the details of the sanctioned housing i n the State of Maharashtra under the said \nscheme; and \n(c)  the status of the scheme under the Wardha and Amravati districts of the State of \nMaharashtra?  \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI) \n \n(a) Yes Sir. \n \n(b) In order to achieve the objective of “Housing f or All”, the erstwhile rural housing scheme \nIndira Awaas Yojana (IAY) has been restructured int o Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana- Gramin \n(PMAY-G) w.e.f. 1 \nst  April, 2016.  A total of 9,88,041 houses have been  sanctioned under \nPMAY-G in the State of Maharashtra.  \n \n(c) The status of PMAY-G Scheme in Wardha and Amrav ati districts of the State of \nMaharashtra is as follows:  \n  \n(units in nos.) \nDistrict Houses Sanctioned Houses Completed \nWardha 13,072 9,409 \nAmravati 68,405 46,035 \n \n***** ",
