    "ls|LS17_S6_U_419": "LOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 4{9\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2OfHJttLY,2O21\nBENEFICIARIES UNDER ONORG\n4{9. SHRI NALIN KUMAR KATEEL:\nWill the llllinister of GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC\nDISTRIBUTIoN 5trsfrmr erri, qr sit{ srffif,fi F{wr d'+ be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether the Supreme Gourt has directed all the States to\nimplememnt One Nation One Ration Gard system (ONORC) recently, if so,\nthe details thereof;\n(b) whether the ONORC Scheme implementation has covered 86% of\nbeneficiaries across 32 States and UTsr if sor the details thereof;\n(c) the names of the remaining States yet to be integrated in the\nscheme, State-wise;\n(e) whether the Government has reviewed the progress of\nimplementation of this scheme, if so, the details thereoti and\n(0 the steps taken to eliminate bogus, ineligible ration cards and reduce\nleakage to make the PDS system better?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT AND\nGONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION\n(SADHVI NIRANJAN JYOTI)\n(a): Yes sir. The Hon'ble Supreme Court of lndia in its iudgement dated\n29-06-20i21 in connection with Suo Motu Writ Petition (Givil) No. 6 ol 2O2O\ntitled 'Problems and Miseries of Migrant Labourers' has also directed the\nStates which have not implemented the One Nation One Ration Gard to\nimptement the same by not later than 31'07'2021.\n.....21-\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIG DISTRIBUTION\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIG DISTRIBUTION\n(d) the number of beneficiaries covered so far, Statewise;\n\n-2-\n(b): Upto Decembot 2O2O the One Nation One Ration Gard (ONORG) plan\nhas been enabled in 32 States/UTs covering about 867\" NFSA population\n(nearly 69 Grore of total 8O Grore beneficiaries) in the country to have an\noption to lift their foodgrains from any Fair Price Shop of choice anyrwhere\nin these 32 States/UT.\n(c): 4 States/UT of Assam, Ghhattisgarhr Delhi and West Bengal are yet to\nenable the ONORG plan.\n(d): A State/UT wlse statement showing number of NFSA beneficlarles\ncovered under OI{ORG plan is at Annexure-!.\n(e): The Department regularly reviews the implementation of OI{ORG\nplan, number of portability transactionsr efforts made by States/UTs\nthrough centrat portals, VG moetingsr letters from all levels to concerned\nStates/UTs and technical partnensr etc.\n(0: As per Targeted Public Distribution System (Gontrol) Order, 2Ol5\nunder National Food Security Act (NFSA), all States/UTs are required to\nreview their list of eligible beneficiaries every year and are required to\nremove/detete the ineligible or bogus ration cards/beneficiaries from their\nration card's database.\n\nAnnexure-l\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF THE UNSTARRED\nOUESTTON NO.4{9 FOR AI{SWER ON 2O.O7.2O2{ !N THE LOK SABHA.\nstate/uT wise statement showing number of NFSA beneficiaries covered under oNoRC\nplan in 32 States/UTs up to December 2020:\nst. Stat'e/UT\nONORC\nlmplementation\nStatus\nNo. of NFSA Beneficiaries\n- All covercd under\nONORC\n(in Lakhs)\nI Andaman and Nicobar lsland lmplemented 0.6'1\n2 Andhra Pradesh lmplemented 268.23\n3 Arunachal Pradesh lmplemented 8.21\n4 Pending 0.00\n5 Bihar lmplemented 864.50\nChandigarh lmplemented 2.75\n7 Chhattisgarh Pending 0.00\nR Dadra Nagar Haveli & Daman Diu lmplemented 2.85\nI Delhi Pending 0.00\n10 Goa lmplemented 5.32\n11 Gujarat lmplemented 382.54\n12 Haryana lmplemented 126.49\n13 Himachal Prader;h lmplemented 28.64\n14 Jammu & Kashnrir lmplemented 72.41\nJharkhand lmplemented 263.70\nlo Karnataka lmplemented 401.93\n17 Kerala lmplemented 154.80\n18 Ladakh lmplemented 1.44\n19 Lakshadweep lmplemented 0.22\n20 Madhya Pradesh lmplemented 546.42\nMaharashtra lmplemented 700.17\n22 Manipur lmplemented 24.57\n23 Meghalaya lmplemented 21.46\n24 Mizoram lmplemented\n25 Nagaland lmplemented \"t4.05\n26 Odisha lmplemented\n27 Puducherry 6.28\n.....21\nAssam\n15\n21\n6.68\n323.60\nlmplemented\n\n-2-\n28 Punjab lmplemented 14