    "ls|LS17_S6_U_461": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.461 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021 \n \nLOSSES TO FARMERS DUE TO LOOSE HIGH-TENSION WIRES \n \n461.  SHRI PRATHAP SIMHA: \nSHRI ANNASAHEB SHANKAR JOLLE: \nDR. UMESH G. JADHAV: \n \n Will the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the farmers of the country are facing huge losses every year due to fire in the \nfields because of loose high -tension wires and if so, the details of incidents reported during the \nlast three years, State-wise; \n \n(b)  whether the Government proposes some compensation to the farmers for loss due to \nelectric fire and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  the mechanism for calculation of loss and the amount of compensation paid so far during \nthe said period, State-wise; \n \n(d)  whether the Government proposes to formulate any policy to review the  mechanism for \ncalculation of loss to give adequate compensation to the farmers; and \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF POWER AND NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY  \n \n(SHRI  R.K. SINGH) \n \n(a) to (e) :  No  such incident of fire has been reported in the lines owned by Inter State \nTransmission licensees including Power Grid Corporation of India Ltd during the last 3 years due to \nloose high tension wires of transmission lines. Various regulations and standa rds for safe \nconstruction, operation & maintenance of electricity infrastructure including for HT lines viz. \nminimum ground clearance, support structures, right of way, span, sag and tension, etc. have been \nnotified by the Government of India/ Electricity Regulatory Commissions/State Power Departments \nto be strictly adhered to by the Distribution and Transmission Utilities. \nIn addition, the Government of India through Skill India has taken initiative to train the \nlinemen of the DISCOMs to help them maintain the infrastructure created. \nElectricity is a concurrent subject and distribution of electricity falls primarily under the \npurview of the respective State Governments and it is the responsibility of the respective State \nPower Utility to operate and maintai n the electricity infrastructure in proper condition. \nAccordingly, the compensation for losses caused by any electricity accidents including fire in the \nfields caused by loose high-tension wires falls within the domain of the State Government/Utilities \nand is decided by the respective State Government/State Power Utility as per their policies in this \nregard. \nInformation in this regard was sought from all the States. However, only State of \nKarnataka, so far, has reported that they have paid compensation amou nting to Rs. 136 lakh \ntowards 352 incidents of fire in the field related to loose high -tension wires of the Distribution \nCompanies, as per their State policy during the periods 2018-19 to 2020-21. \n******** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_462": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK\n \nSABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 462\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 22.07.2021\n \n \nOpening of Agro Industry\n \n \n462. \n \nSHRI HANUMAN BENIWAL\n: \n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND\n \nMEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government proposes to open/start Agro Industry in the Atmanirbhar Bharat \nAbhiyaan keeping in mind the number of agriculture graduates passing out every year; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(\nc) \n \nwhether the Government intends to set up any agro industry in Rajasthan as the large \nnumber of population is engaged in agriculture and spices and other agro products; and\n \n \n(d) \n \nif\n \nso, the details thereof along with the time by which the said industry is likely to be set \nup in Rajasthan and if not, the reasons therefor?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NARAYAN RANE)\n \n \n(a)\n \n&\n \n(b)\n:\n \nGovernment in the Ministry of MSME is implementing since 2008\n-\n09, Prime \nMinister’s Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP) which is a major credit\n-\nlinked subsidy \nprogramme aimed at generating self\n-\nemployment opportunities through establishment of micro\n-\nent\nerprises in the non\n-\nfarm sector by helping traditional artisans and rural/urban unemployed \nyouth. The \nScheme is in line with the \nAtmanirbhar Bharat Abhiyaan as it encourages setting up of \nnew micro\n-\nenterprises using local raw material and rural workforce.\n \nThe maximum cost of \nprojects is Rs.25 lakh in the manufacturing sector and Rs.10 lakh in the service sector with \nsubsidy varying from 15% to 35% for different categories. \n \n \nAny \nindividual can apply for PMEGP through online portal \nwww.kviconline.gov.in\n. \nEmphasis has also been given to reach out to students in various Universities including \nagriculture \ngraduates, to generate awareness about the scheme and encourage them to apply under it.\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n: 2 :\n \n \n \n \nThe number of\n \nunits assisted, disbursement of margin money and employment generated \nunder PMEGP across the country during last three years and current year is as follows:\n \nYear\n \nNo. of units \nset up**\n \nMargin Money \ndisbursed \n \n(Rs. in crore)\n \nEstimated \nEmployment \n \n(Nos.)\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n73427\n \n2070.00\n \n587416\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n66653\n \n1950.82\n \n533224\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n74415\n \n2188.80\n \n595320\n \n2021\n-\n22 \n \n(as on 09.07.2021)\n \n16639\n \n518.25\n \n133112\n \nTotal\n \n231134\n \n6727.87\n \n1849072\n \n(**\nFigure of Year\n-\nwise \nno. of units set up indicate the no. of units for which the MM has been disbursed to \nthe banks in the respective FY)\n \nAbout 25% of the\n \nunits setup under PMEGP belongs to agro and forest based industries.\n \n \n \n(c) \n& (d)\n:\n \nTarget and achievement for the last \nthree years to set up micro\n-\nenterprises under \nPMEGP\n \nin Rajasthan is as follows:\n \n \nSl\n.\n \nYear\n \nTarget\n \nAchievement \n \n \n \nNo. of Units \nset up\n \nMM \n(Rs. in \nlakh)\n \nEmploym\nent (Nos.)\n \nNo. of units \nset up\n \nMM (Rs. \nin lakh)\n \nEmploym\nent (Nos.)\n \n1\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n3097\n \n7743.65\n \n24776\n \n2359\n \n7199.28\n \n18872\n \n2\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n3398\n \n10194.20\n \n27184\n \n3025\n \n8174.68\n \n24200\n \n3\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n2697\n \n8094.02\n \n21576\n \n2772\n \n8806.83\n \n22176\n \n \nBased on the dynamic situation arising out of COVID\n-\n19 challenges and the previous years’ \nperformance, the approximate target for setting up PMEGP units during FY 2021\n-\n22 and \nachievement thereon in the state of Rajasthan is as follows: \n \n \nTarget\n \nAchievement\n \n(as on 9.7.2021)\n \nNo. of Units \nset up\n \nMM (Rs. in \nlakh)\n \nEmployment \n(Nos.)\n \nNo. of units \nset up\n \nMM \n \n(Rs. in lakh)\n \nEmployment \n(Nos.)\n \n3500\n \n10500.00\n \n28000\n \n305\n \n1216.50\n \n2440\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n: 3 :\n \n \n \n \nIn addition, Ministry is also implementing \nScheme of Fund for Regeneration of \nTraditional Industries (SFURTI). \nThe focus of the scheme is to organize traditional industries \nand artisans into clusters and provide them with sustainable employment by making their products \nmore competitive through valu\ne addition. Under the scheme, artisans are collectively supported \nthrough construction of Common Facility Centres (CFCs), new plants and machineries, training, \netc. in sectors\n \nsuch as Agro Based Industries, Honey, Khadi, Coir, Handicrafts, Textiles, Bamboo\n \netc. \n \n \nAs on 19.07.2021, 433 clusters have been approved benefitting about 2.6 lakh artisan with \nGoI assistance of Rs.1102 crore.\n \n \nIn \nRajasthan, 27 clusters have been approved under SFURTI benefitting about 15284 \nartisans with GoI assistance of 75.20 cror\ne. Of these 10 clusters are in agro processing, bamboo \nand honey. These clusters are likely to be functional within a period of 12 to 18 months from date \nof approval.\n \n \n \n*****\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
